message.content:
{
  "paraphrase": "For every function f from the natural numbers to the natural numbers, if f is equal to the multiset function defined as the cardinality of the set of multisets M where each element m in M is a factorial of some integer k between 1 and n, and the sum of all elements in M equals n factorial, then for every natural number n greater than or equal to 2, there exists a real number C such that the inequality n raised to the power of (n squared divided by 2 minus C times n) multiplied by the exponential of negative (n squared divided by 4) is less than or equal to f(n), and f(n) is less than or equal to n raised to the power of (n squared divided by 2 plus C times n) multiplied by the exponential of negative (n squared divided by 4)."
}
